Description: Tools for importing, processing, analysing, and visualising
    single-cell spatial biology data from multiplexed imaging platforms.
    Supports cell-table quality control, marker normalisation, phenotype
    summaries, spatial neighbourhood statistics such as Ripley's K function
    (Ripley (1977) <doi:10.1111/j.2517-6161.1977.tb01615.x>) and Moran's I
    (Moran (1950) <doi:10.2307/2332142>), and explicit sample and
    coordinate-frame registries. Patient-level inference enumerates label
    allocations for declared contrasts (exact permutation tests; Pitman
    (1937) <doi:10.2307/2984124>) and retains unavailable hypotheses when
    adjusting for multiple testing. Grouped summaries expose missingness,
    eligibility, and denominator provenance. Optional canonical cell-table
    import uses 'cellspecR' <https://github.com/CTTIR/cellspecR>; optional
    Self-Organising Nebulous Growths (SONG) embeddings (Senanayake et al.
    (2021) <doi:10.1109/TNNLS.2020.3023941>) use 'songR'
    <https://github.com/CTTIR/songR>. Both optional packages are available
    from <https://cttir.r-universe.dev>.
